<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="060" project="spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI">
  <metadata>
    <title>ArchTest: ban new secret-bearing confidential clients (FR-F1)</title>
    <phase>6 Forcing Functions</phase>
    <gate>022 complete</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies tests/**; TEST-MODIFYING override makes code-review + adr-check unconditional.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Structural test with an existing in-repo pattern to copy.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>G</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>022</deps>
    <tags>testing,auth,archtest,forcing-function</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add an ArchTest that fails the build when any type under src/server/** calls .WithClientSecret or constructs ClientSecretCredential outside a named allowlist. This is the mechanism that stops the project's core failure from recurring.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer with NetArchTest experience.</role>
  <goal>A CI-enforced ban with a documented allowlist and a proven negative control.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>The predecessor audit inventoried all nine secret consumers correctly and then concluded NEVER-REMOVE on a false premise. Text was corrected in 2026-08-17 but text is what failed last time. ADR-028 E-3 explicitly states adr-check should cite E-3 for listed sites and STILL FLAG any NEW .WithClientSecret site — this test is that rule in executable form.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/CredentialGuardTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/GodClassGuardTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/LayerDependencyTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies><dependency task="022" status="pending">The end-state credential shape to assert against</dependency></dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: the allowlist contains ONLY E-1 sites (SpeAdminTokenProvider, SpeAdminGraphService — other applications' identities) and E-3 sites until task 033 completes. Each entry carries a written reason.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: copy the GodClassGuardTests shape — ratchet with a documented maintenance procedure, not a hard-coded absolute.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: this is an ArchTest (source/assembly analysis), NOT a DI-registration test. Ban B3 applies.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: include a NEGATIVE CONTROL proving the detector actually fires, the way LayerDependencyTests does at :81.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: ALSO add the decoupling guard deferred from task 010 -- assert by SOURCE ANALYSIS that DataverseAccessDataSource never assigns _cca inside the managed-identity branch. Task 010 decoupled the app-only credential from the OBO confidential client; a future "simplification" back to a single if/else would set _cca = null whenever MI is enabled and silently disable OBO -- a total fail-closed outage. This guard could not live in the seam test: reading those private fields is ADR-038 ban B8 (reflection), and the class swallows credential errors into AccessRights.None so selection is not observable behaviourally. Source analysis is the sanctioned shape and is stronger -- it fails at the shape level, not on one sampled configuration. See notes/decisions/010-credential-gating.md §4.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: Power BI (ReportingEmbedService, ReportingProfileManager, PowerBiOptions) is an ALLOWLIST entry with the reason "Workstream D deferred 2026-08-19 -- Power BI not yet adopted at Spaarke; PowerBi:ClientSecret is a separate secret from BFF-API-ClientSecret and does not gate the OBO migration. Revisit when Power BI is adopted (tasks 040-042)." Do NOT leave it as an unexplained exemption and do NOT let the detector over-fire on it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: ALLOWLIST OrderedCredentialClientProvider AS THE SANCTIONED .WithClientSecret BINDING POINT, WITH ITS REASON. Booked by task 021 (implemented 2026-08-21). The ordered selector necessarily contains a .WithClientSecret call — it is the E-3 transitional fallback and the rollback target, and a selector without it cannot express the rollback NFR-06 depends on. It is CONSOLIDATION, not expansion: task 022 removes the four existing sites and routes them through this one, and task 033 deletes the branch. Without an allowlist entry, the forcing function this project exists to leave behind would fail on the very mechanism that makes the secret removable. The entry MUST carry the reason inline, exactly like the Power BI deferral entry — an unexplained allowlist entry is how the next audit concludes the secret is permanent.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: DISCHARGED, DO NOT RE-DIAGNOSE. An earlier revision of this POML booked "diagnose the task-020 seam flake" onto this task. It was resolved at tasks 023/024 and it was NOT a flake: the test asserted MsalServiceException while MSAL throws MsalClientException for managed_identity_all_sources_unavailable, and task 021's fall-through predicate and catch clause carried the SAME wrong assumption -- so a host with no IMDS would have failed the request instead of falling through to the secret. Fixed in both places, with regression tests pinning the shape MSAL actually throws. Recorded here so this task does not spend effort re-investigating a closed item. See notes/decisions/021-credential-config-keys.md section 13a.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: ADD A SOURCE-ANALYSIS GUARD THAT NO MANAGED IDENTITY IS RESOLVED BY NAME. Booked by task 023. The dev subscription holds five UAMIs and one (spaarke-bff-identity) is named as though it were the BFF's without being attached to it; the BFF's actual identity is mi-bff-api-dev. Name-based resolution would pick the decoy and fail only at token exchange. Verified at task 023 that the runtime does NOT do this today -- a grep of src/ for either identity name returns exactly one hit, a doc comment warning about the decoy -- but that is a fact about the current source, not a guard. This is source analysis (the shape ADR-038 sanctions, and the shape this task already builds), not a runtime test.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>NetArchTest, forcing functions</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>tests/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/god-class-ratchet.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Read GodClassGuardTests and LayerDependencyTests for the ratchet + negative-control conventions.</step>
    <step>Implement the detector over src/server/** for .WithClientSecret and ClientSecretCredential.</step>
    <step>Build the allowlist from ADR-028 E-1 and E-3, each with a reason.</step>
    <step>Add the negative control.</step>
    <step>Document the maintenance procedure in the test's own comment, as the sibling tests do.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The detector cannot distinguish E-1 sites from BFF-identity sites reliably — STOP; a test that over-fires will be suppressed and the mechanism lost.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="new">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/CredentialGuardTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>A new .WithClientSecret site outside the allowlist FAILS the build.</criterion>
    <criterion>Existing E-1 sites pass without modification.</criterion>
    <criterion>The negative control proves the detector fires on a seeded violation.</criterion>
    <criterion>A seeded re-entanglement of DataverseAccessDataSource (assigning _cca inside the MI branch) FAILS the build.</criterion>
    <criterion>Every allowlist entry carries a written reason and an ADR reference.</criterion>
    <criterion>The Power BI sites are allowlisted with the deferral reason recorded verbatim, and a future un-deferral is a one-line allowlist removal.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative case: the test does NOT fire on CiamGraphClientFactory (certificate) or on the new assertion provider.</criterion>
    <criterion>The maintenance procedure is documented in the test file itself.</criterion>
      <!-- Booked 2026-08-21 by task 020 (code-review/adr-check finding W1). Task 020's seam tests
         could not assert that the signed assertion is REUSED rather than re-minted per call: the DI
         half is ADR-038 ban B3, and the per-instance half is compiler-enforced (readonly field), so a
         runtime test asserts either a banned shape or a tautology. Source analysis is the right
         instrument and this task is the one that has it -- previously this deferral pointed here
         without 060 actually accepting it. -->
    <criterion>Source analysis asserts that ManagedIdentityClientAssertion is constructed ONLY in a constructor or static initializer, never inside a method body. A per-call construction would re-mint a signed assertion (an IMDS round trip) on every token acquisition, silently converting the singleton registration from load-bearing to decorative -- the exact regression ADR-028 A4's "reuse the instance" rule exists to prevent.</criterion>
    <criterion>Negative control for that rule: a scratch provider that news up the assertion inside GetAssertionAsync FAILS the check.</criterion>
</acceptance-criteria>
  <notes>
    Completed 2026-08-21. Record: notes/decisions/060-credential-guard.md

    SUCCESS CRITERION 12 DEMONSTRATED LIVE: a scratch ninth secret-bearing confidential client was
    added under Infrastructure/Auth and the guard failed the build naming file:line and the form of
    binding; the file was then removed and ArchTests returned to 44/44.

    Two stale POML references corrected: GodClassGuardTests.cs does not exist (LOC ratchet RETIRED
    2026-08-20, root CLAUDE.md 11.5) - conventions taken from LayerDependencyTests and
    DataverseServiceClientDowncastTests instead; and the _cca field no longer exists after task 022,
    so the 010 decoupling guard is expressed against the post-022 shape (OboAvailable must not
    consult the MI flag; the OBO fields must not be assigned inside the app-only branch).

    Allowlist: 5 entries (provider E-3, SpeAdminTokenProvider + SpeAdminGraphService E-1, Power BI x2
    with the deferral reason verbatim). A second test FAILS if any entry lacks a substantive reason or
    an ADR citation - the allowlist is the part that decays.

    The negative controls found two real defects in my own detector: line-scoped analysis flagged the
    SANCTIONED multi-line-ternary assertion assignment, and after switching to statement-scoping,
    brace boundaries were still needed or the ctor signature prefixed the assignment. Both were caught
    by the positive control, not by reading.

    ArchTests 44/44 (36 + 8 new).
  </notes>
</task>
